# Factual scope of the floor-presence39 fixture controller

This source-only clarification corrects an overstatement in the immutable
`.build/cyd-vorbis-floor-presence-runtime-prep-01/README.md`. Its description of
an inherited "QMP lifecycle" is incorrect. The planning description in immutable
generator02 `DESIGN.md` also must not be read as evidence that a QMP lifecycle or
complete configured compiler-dependency walk was implemented in this fixture.
The executable source is authoritative. Both preparations remain byte-exact.
This note changes no source, input, witness, metric, threshold or recorded result.

## Implemented controller behavior

`controller.template.py` inherits the earlier mono21 nine-command controller.
Its ordered actual command roles are `sdk-head`, `sdk-clean`, `build`,
`setup-macros`, `symbols`, `merge`, `qemu`, `sdk-head-after`, `sdk-clean-after`.
It records each owned command's argv, cwd, PID, terminal status, timeout /
interruption state and stdout/stderr hashes. Nonzero exits fail the controller.

It launches QEMU directly with serial stdio, no display or monitor, `-no-reboot`,
`-snapshot`, `-nic none`, two emulated cores and the isolated merged flash image.
It waits for the owned QEMU process's real terminal exit and then validates the
complete serial protocol. It does not open QMP, negotiate QMP capabilities, send
quit, verify a quit acknowledgement, or record a QMP SHUTDOWN/EOF lifecycle.
There is no QMP helper in this capsule.

Before the target runs, the controller verifies and snapshots the explicit
candidate setup/output bridge, caller/project files, raw corpus / contract /
materialized header, reference proofs / binding and active Python helpers. It
records tool/archive/ROM hashes and checks those identities using `current()`.
It checks SDK HEAD and tracked SDK cleanliness before and after execution. It
requires the expected vendor archive identities, actual Xtensa ELF machine94,
one frozen caller compile row and the two expected bridge compile rows.

The actual setup macro probe uses its recorded compile row and two generated
compiler-input files; those two files are frozen and checked before and after
the probe. It requires ESP32, repair enabled,240MHz, two-core and unrestricted
format macros. It checks the wrapper/decoder symbols and the isolated flash
recipe / offsets. These are explicit compile-context checks. They do not form a
complete compiler dependency walk or a full snapshot of the configured SDK /
transitive source tree. This capsule has no such dependency-walk stage.

The controller's `current()` rehashes every explicit report input and its frozen
copy, each recorded tool/archive/ROM, and all recorded variant source members.
Before successful completion it separately rehashes every recorded
`build_outputs` member. It validates all1212 protocol events, full consumption,
metadata, canaries, overlap frame counts, uint64 case mask and all per-frame
silence/nonzero witnesses. It persists all39 target PCM files and checks their
exact bytes, hashes, offsets, file set and971520-byte total. Actual success must
still be established by root execution; source inspection alone is not success.

## Implemented independent numerical replay

`capture39.py` requires the actual completed target report and direct-tool
terminal0 bound to the sealed controller before interpreting target PCM. It
checks the runtime preparation / exact counts, reconstructs the controller from
the reviewed template and actual runtime facts, checks all nine actual command
terminals / log hashes, and rehashes every recorded frozen report input.

It checks the frozen caller and helpers, original and variant setup identities,
the macro evidence, the complete relocated raw contract, every protocol event,
all per-frame silence/nonzero witnesses, and each persisted full PCM file with
its raw-channel / reference metadata, offsets and hash. It canonicalizes the
full `variant_sources` pathname/hash map and rejects duplicate/unsafe names;
its direct variant-file identity check is for setup.c. It does not independently
rehash every `report.tools`, every `report.build_outputs` or every remaining
variant source file. Those broader identity checks are performed by the actual
controller at its completion, as described above; the numerical replay must
not be described as independently repeating all of them.

`compare_capture39.py` then replays all78 recorded reference streams / child
receipts and applies both full-stream comparisons under the unchanged
predeclared2signed-S16LSB bound. This project bound is not a normative Vorbis
tolerance. All reference and target silence witnesses are still mandatory.
No trim, shift, fitting, resampling, padding, channel swap or mono duplication
is applied. This correction introduces no weakened or substituted pass gate.

The intended finite scope remains39 valid floor1 presence cases,546 raw packets,
two reference decoders and the public raw CYD fixture. It is not fullG6, complete
Vorbis conformance, physical performance or production radio integration.
Existing mono21 evidence and unrelated NONPASS results retain their own scope.
The root's actual safe direct-child host output is unaffected; the source review
also noted that the generic host output guard does not prohibit nesting output
inside its source directory, which is outside the documented current invocation.
No such nested output is used or endorsed by this finite workflow.

This note was prepared by source / metadata reading and hashing only, before
target execution. It does not claim a future target or numerical outcome.
